{"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Segment-trees","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree"],"title":"Segment trees","generated":true}],"abstract":[{"text":"A segment tree with lazy propagation: a sequence of values that combines any range of them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under a monoid and applies an update to every value in a range, each in O(log ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SH","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/ST"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LazySegmentTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MonoidAction","preciseIdentifier":"s:10RangeTrees12MonoidActionP"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The layout is "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"‘s: a perfect binary tree over the values padded to a power of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two, in one flat array of cells. Beside each internal cell sits a pending update, applied to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that cell’s value but not yet to the cells below it. A range update applies itself to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") cells that cover the range and leaves it pending there, pushing older pending"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"updates down one level on the way so that updates reach each cell in the order they were made."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A query reads without changing the tree, composing the pending updates of the cells it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passes through."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" names the monoid and the updates:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["enum AddToSum: MonoidAction {","    typealias Values = Sum<Int>","    static var identity: Int { 0 }","    static func compose(_ outer: Int, _ inner: Int) -> Int { outer + inner }","    static func apply(_ update: Int, to sum: Int, count: Int) -> Int { sum + update * count }","}","","var tree = LazySegmentTree<AddToSum>([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])","tree.apply(10, in: 1 ..< 4)","tree.combined(in: 0 ..< 5)   \/\/ 45","tree[2]                      \/\/ 13"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"As a collection, a lazy segment tree’s elements are the values, in order, with every update","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applied.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:10RangeTrees15LazySegmentTreeV","remoteSource":{"fileName":"LazySegmentTree.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree.swift#L31"},"title":"LazySegmentTree","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LazySegmentTree"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LazySegmentTree"}],"modules":[{"name":"RangeTrees"}]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/init()","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/init(_:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/apply(_:checkedIn:)","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/apply(_:in:)","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/combined(checkedIn:)","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/combined(in:)","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/update(at:to:)","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/update(checkedAt:to:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true},{"anchor":"Subscripts","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/subscript(checked:)"],"title":"Subscripts","generated":true},{"anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/Element","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/Update"],"title":"Type Aliases","generated":true},{"anchor":"Default-Implemen